cellations are below 1%, and the Halbrook plant is back at full capacity after the fire. Management expects to recover the lost shipments by mid-2027, which would add volume in H1 2027. This view puts revenue at about C$4.1–4.2B.\n- **Case against (industry data):** Industry shipments fell 4% in Q2 2026, the first decline in three years. Voltaris shipments fell 9%, and its share of Caldrian transformer shipments dropped from 31% to 27%. This view puts revenue at about C$3.4–3.6B.\n- **The stretch required:** The last four quarters sum to C$3.735B, so guidance needs about 12% growth. It also needs about C$1.05B a quarter, against a best recent quarter of C$980M.\n- **How I weighed them:** Backlog is not revenue, and I don't know how much of it is scheduled for 2027 delivery. The industry-share view rests on thin data and ignores pricing, mix and non-Caldrian sales. The two views sit far apart, which suggests the backlog is partly offsetting the share loss.\n\nNeither sub-analysis found Q3 2026 results or any other 2027 disclosures. The two things that would settle it are how much of the backlog ships in 2027 and whether Voltaris has stopped losing share.\n\nThe detail is in n2.r1 (company disclosures) and n3.r1 (industry data).","ttft_ms":1799,"type":"result","duration_ms":38068,"uuid":"f487ca43-cfb4-4b53-8577-3320c64c62fb","ttft_stream_ms":1253,"time_to_request_ms":169,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":9,"system_prompt":20,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":10,"input_attachments":53,"input_hooks":7,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":7,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":13,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":10,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":4,"tool_schema_build":10,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":4,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":43,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":86,"time_to_req